{"uid":"modules/shell_session_store.py","name":"shell_session_store.py","qualname":"modules/shell_session_store.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/shell_session_store.py","line":1,"end_line":254,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Resumable, hash-identified shell session descriptors.","description":"A remote shell is a live socket that dies with the process that opened it, so\nit cannot be serialized and reloaded. What survives is the *descriptor*: which\ntarget yielded the shell, through which exploit primitive, on which port, from\nwhich attacker address, and when. This module persists one JSON descriptor per\nsession under a content-hashed id and re-opens the shell through the recorded\nprimitive on :func:`resume` -- the same reconnection model serious\npost-exploitation frameworks use over non-persistent transports.\n\nThe store is deliberately decoupled from the transport: it imports\n:mod:`modules.atomic_exploit_bridge` lazily and only inside :func:`resume`, so\nregistering a descriptor never pulls the socket layer and cannot deadlock the\nloop. Every public function is fail-open: persistence or I/O errors degrade to\nan empty result instead of raising into a campaign.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/shell_session_store.py::ID_LENGTH","modules/shell_session_store.py::STATUS_LIVE","modules/shell_session_store.py::STATUS_STALE","modules/shell_session_store.py::STATUS_CLOSED","modules/shell_session_store.py::session_id","modules/shell_session_store.py::register","modules/shell_session_store.py::get","modules/shell_session_store.py::list_sessions","modules/shell_session_store.py::mark_closed","modules/shell_session_store.py::resume"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
